# ABOUTME: Declares what `use Class::Struct` exports: struct, bare.
# ABOUTME: Measured on perl 5.42.0 with Class::Struct 0.68: struct carries no prototype.
package Class::Struct;

# struct takes a plain slurpy list (its shape, a class name plus an
# array- or hash-style element list, or just the element list, is not a
# prototype perl states). It ends `carp $@ if $@;`: measured on 5.42.0,
# when the generated accessors eval cleanly (the ordinary case) that
# statement modifier's value is the empty Str, and when they do not, it
# is carp's Boolean.
sub struct :export (List @args) Str|Boolean;
